# System: the flow algebra
#
# Workflow composition is right-skewed — from the flow doc (read in full).

#>spw_system_flow_algebra
#:system #!form

^"the_fact"{
  ~#skew: "choice does not left-distribute over composition — the half (P⋆R)⊔(Q⋆R) ≤ (P⊔Q)⋆R holds; the converse FAILS"
  ~#structure: "a right-skewed Kleene algebra with distributive meets — RSKA, Pradic's Weihrauch-lattice structure, landed on the real workflow executor"
  @doc: ~"../../metatheory/docs/FLOW-COMPOSITION-ALGEBRA.md"
}

^"why_it_is_real"{
  ~#order: "the order is ONLINE step-by-step simulation, not trace language — on the separating counterexample the trace languages are provably EQUAL; a language-only semantics would wrongly conclude distribution; the skew lives one rung up"
  ~#cause: "the late branch reads R's output before choosing; the early branch has already committed — the obstruction is precisely no-lookahead, the reactive gate's old+new read"
}

^"the_payoff"{
  ~#decidable: "flow/policy refinement A ≤ B becomes a Büchi simulation game — decidable, known complexity; the protocol-evolution bar inherits a decision procedure resting on a proof, not a hope" =frontier
}
